{UTF-8}
{ Chapter 11: orders respond to price and to delivery delay through two normalised effects. A price cut at week 10 pushes orders above capacity; the backlog and the delivery delay rise until the delay effect brings orders back to capacity. }
Normal Orders=
	100
	~	units/week
	~	Orders per week at the reference price and the normal delivery delay.
	|
Reference Price=
	50
	~	dollars/unit
	~	The price customers compare against.
	|
Price Change=
	0
	~	dmnl
	~	Fractional change in price at week 10 (-0.2 is a 20% cut).
	|
Price Change Time=
	10
	~	week
	~	|
Price=
	Reference Price * (1 + STEP(Price Change, Price Change Time))
	~	dollars/unit
	~	|
Relative Price=
	Price / Reference Price
	~	dmnl
	~	|
Effect of Price on Orders table(
	[(0,0)-(3,2)],(0,2),(0.5,1.8),(0.75,1.4),(1,1),(1.25,0.65),(1.5,0.4),(2,0.15),(3,0.05))
	~	dmnl
	~	Normalised: 1 at the reference price; slope -1.6 below and -1.4 above, so the elasticity at the normal point is about -1.5.
	|
Effect of Price on Orders=
	Effect of Price on Orders table(Relative Price)
	~	dmnl
	~	|
Normal Delivery Delay=
	4
	~	week
	~	The delivery delay customers expect.
	|
Perception Time=
	4
	~	week
	~	Time customers take to notice a change in delivery delay.
	|
Perceived Delivery Delay=
	SMOOTH(Delivery Delay, Perception Time)
	~	week
	~	|
Relative Delivery Delay=
	Perceived Delivery Delay / Normal Delivery Delay
	~	dmnl
	~	|
Effect of Delay on Orders table(
	[(0,0)-(4,2)],(0,1.05),(0.5,1.03),(1,1),(1.5,0.9),(2,0.75),(3,0.5),(4,0.35))
	~	dmnl
	~	Normalised: 1 at the normal delay; flat near the normal point, falling as delays lengthen.
	|
Effect of Delay on Orders=
	Effect of Delay on Orders table(Relative Delivery Delay)
	~	dmnl
	~	|
Additive Combination=
	0
	~	dmnl
	~	1: combine the effects by adding their deviations; 0: multiply them.
	|
Combined Effect=
	IF THEN ELSE(Additive Combination = 1, 1 + (Effect of Price on Orders - 1) + (Effect of Delay on Orders - 1), Effect of Price on Orders * Effect of Delay on Orders)
	~	dmnl
	~	|
Orders=
	Normal Orders * Combined Effect
	~	units/week
	~	|
Normal Capacity=
	120
	~	units/week
	~	|
Capacity Change=
	0
	~	dmnl
	~	Fractional change in capacity (-0.6 is a 60% loss).
	|
Capacity Change Time=
	10
	~	week
	~	|
Capacity=
	Normal Capacity * (1 + STEP(Capacity Change, Capacity Change Time))
	~	units/week
	~	|
Target Delivery Delay=
	4
	~	week
	~	The delay the firm plans to ship within; equal to what customers expect.
	|
Desired Shipments=
	Backlog / Target Delivery Delay
	~	units/week
	~	|
Shipments=
	MIN(Desired Shipments, Capacity)
	~	units/week
	~	|
Delivery Delay=
	ZIDZ(Backlog, Shipments)
	~	week
	~	|
Initial Backlog=
	400
	~	units
	~	Set to Normal Orders * Normal Delivery Delay for a start in balance.
	|
Backlog= INTEG(
	Orders - Shipments,
	Initial Backlog)
	~	units
	~	|
INITIAL TIME = 0 ~ week ~ |
FINAL TIME = 100 ~ week ~ |
TIME STEP = 0.0625 ~ week ~ |
SAVEPER = 0.0625 ~ week ~ |
